# This project's evidence is hash-verified, and `m4/rules.py` and `m5/ledger.py`
# must stay byte-identical to their canonical copies in Taiwan Core -- a test
# asserts it. So line endings are normalised in the repository (LF) and left to
# the platform on checkout, which is what `core.autocrlf` was already doing.
#
# Do not add `eol=lf` here. It was tried on 2026-09-01 and immediately broke the
# mirror: it rewrote rules.py from CRLF to LF on checkout, 24,902 bytes became
# 24,274, and the upstream parity test is the only thing that would have caught
# it. Declaring an intent is not free when something downstream hashes bytes.
* text=auto

# Archived evidence and vendor exports: byte-exact or they are not evidence.
*.pdf     binary
*.zip     binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.xls     binary
*.parquet binary
*.duckdb  binary
